WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:08.941
Private software needs an access policy. This controls who can
open encrypted files, without giving them permission to
administer your fleet.

2
00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:17.103
Open Access policies before publishing confidential software.
These rules control decryption, not fleet administration.

3
00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:24.154
Choose Group and select the intended group. Its membership
determines which devices may request access keys.

4
00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:31.767
The grant is saved. Removing access stops future key requests;
it cannot erase files that were already decrypted.

5
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:39.303
The access rule is saved. Use it when publishing a confidential
release, and review membership as your fleet changes.
